    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "2007842452217205243",
      "url": "https://x.com/ISSF_India/status/2007842452217205243",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/ISSF_India/status/2007842452217205243",
      "text": "In 25 years, India has flipped the script on Defence Production.\n\nWe went from buying 70% of our security to building 75% of it.\n\nThe infographic below isn’t just a curve; it’s the timeline of India’s strategic autonomy.\n\nHere’s the breakdown of the shift.👇\n\nThe Starting Line (2000):\n\nPost-Kargil war, the reality was harsh.\n\n• Import Dependency: ~70%\n\n• Domestic Share: ~30%\n\n• The Ecosystem: 100% State-run (OFBs/DPSUs).\n\nWe were the world’s largest open chequebook for arms dealers. \n\nThe private sector was virtually locked out.\n\nThe \"Lost Decade\" & The Pivot (2005–2014)\n\nPolicy paralysis slowed the climb.\n\nDespite opening the sector to private players in 2001, we saw \"frameworks\" but no factories.\n\nImports soared as we replaced vintage Soviet gear with modern Western platforms - off - the -shelf. \n\nThe indigenisation needle barely moved past 40%.\n\nThe Catalyst (2015–2020)\n\nThree moves changed the trajectory:\n\n\"Make in India\" (2014): \n\nPrioritized Indian-designed gear (IDDM).\n\nThe \"Negative\" Lists (2020): We banned the import of 5,000+ items (artillery, light tanks, comms). \n\nIf we could make it, we had to buy it local.\n\nFDI Liberalisation: 74% allowed under automatic route.\n\nThe New Reality (2025)\n\nThe curve hits escape velocity.\n\n• Capital Budget for Indian Industry: 75% (Record High)\n\n• Production Value: >₹1.5 Lakh Cr\n\n• Exports: ₹23,000+ Cr (Armenia, Philippines, etc.)\n\nWe aren't just making small \nparts anymore; we are making the platforms (LCH, Tejas, C-295).\n\nThe Takeaway\n\nIt took 25 years to invert the ratio.\n\n• 2000: 70% Imported / 30% Made\n\n• 2025: 25% Imported / 75% Made\n\nThis isn't just about saving forex; it's about supply chain resilience. \n\nIn a crisis, you can't fight with an invoice. You need the factory.\n\nWhat's Next?\n\nThe challenge shifts from \"Can we make it?\" to \"Can we design it?\"\n\nThe next 5 years will be defined by R&D ownership, aero-engines, and bringing the 75% to 90%.",
