    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "2007844374500037010",
      "url": "https://x.com/cst_william/status/2007844374500037010",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/cst_william/status/2007844374500037010",
      "text": "I’ll be fully transparent.\n\n2025 was a year of wins, but also failures.\n\nHere’s a clear breakdown of what happened and where I’m headed in 2026. Public accountability.\n\nFirst, the wins.\n\nPERSONAL\n\n • Traveled across Thailand and Vietnam for 6 months\n\n • Met incredible people along the way\n\n • Solid gym progress (78kg lean at some point this year)\n\n • Read 60+ books and summaries (mostly via Shortform)\n\nBUSINESS\n\n • Scaled Notionbase with a new website, blog, products, and freebies\n\n • Grew the YouTube channel to 10k+ subscribers\n\n • Made $4k in my first year selling digital products (Gumroad + Notion Marketplace)\n\n • Crossed my first $1k/month milestone\n\n • Went from 0 to 1,000 followers on X\n\nNow, the losses.\n\nPERSONAL\n\n • A life-threatening injury in Vietnam\n → Lost 10kg during the months following surgery\n → Took a real mental hit\n → Had to fly back home for insurance and treatment\n\n • Too much scrolling and YouTube (guilty)\n\n • Poor sleep habits\n\n • Inconsistent meditation and breathwork\n\nBUSINESS\n\n • Spent too much time building great products and not enough time marketing them (a.k.a. what moves the money needle)\n\n • Didn’t post as much content and products as planned\n\n • Experimented with algorithmic trading, which led to emotional ups and downs (I lost more than I made). I realized I wasn’t aligned with it and eventually stopped.\n\nStill, this year gave me something more valuable than growth.\n\nClarity.\n\nI’m clearer than ever on what I want to build and why.\n\nI realized I don’t want to tie my entire identity to a single tool like Notion (even though I genuinely love it).\n\nAnd I also don’t want to become another loud “motivational trader” guru chasing attention.\n\nMy mission is simple: help solopreneurs organize their life and business, make more money, and live a more free and aligned life.\n\nAnd most importantly, I want to practice what I preach.\n\nSo here’s what’s next.\n\nPERSONAL\n\n • Going back to working while traveling and intentionally networking (I'm actually flying to the Philippines in 5 days, I'll keep you posted on that).\n\n • After the longest break I’ve taken in 9 years (6 months), I’m committing again to a serious gym and health routine. Fitness has always been my anchor and my gateway to discipline in both life and business, and I really missed it in the second half of the year.\n\nBUSINESS\n\n • Clear separation between my Notion content (Notionbase) and my personal brand as a solopreneur (William Coste)\n\n • Doubling down on my personal brand through:\n – X content\n – A biweekly newsletter (Solopreneur Stories, just launched)\n – A weekly podcast (Solopreneurship, coming soon)\n\n • Long-term goal: build a complete digital products ecosystem: courses, Notion templates, and systems for solopreneurs.\n\nThat’s my plan for 2026.\n\nWhat’s yours?\n\nP.S. Just launched my personal website, all links in bio.\n\n P.P.S. Follow me on X, bookmark this post for updates, and join the newsletter for weekly, honest lessons on solopreneurship, systems, and freedom.\n→ https://t.co/ABl4wXl7SG",
